1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:03,496
A black horse-drawn buggy idles
at a red traffic light on Route

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:06,036
three forty in Intercourse, Pennsylvania,

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:10,260
surrounded by idling suburban
SUVs and modern delivery vans.

4
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:14,276
Behind the buggy stands a three-
story historic fieldstone barn

5
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:16,236
built in the eighteenth century.

6
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:18,876
But the rolling pastures
that once surrounded it

7
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:21,616
are now bordered
by a sprawling shopping outlet,

8
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,636
a suburban housing subdivision,

9
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:27,020
and a hotel catering
to millions of annual tourists.

10
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:31,356
An auction sign stands planted in the
manicured lawn of a neighboring farm,

11
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,796
advertising prime Lancaster
County agricultural soil

12
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:37,376
for more than twenty-five
thousand dollars an acre.

13
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,036
For nearly three centuries,

14
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:41,056
this fertile valley has been the sacred,

15
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:44,640
undisputed heartland of the Old
Order Amish in America.

16
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:45,796
Yet today,

17
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:49,176
hundreds of families are quietly
packing their wooden chests,

18
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:51,156
selling generational homesteads,

19
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:54,876
and boarding hired passenger
vans to leave the state entirely.

20
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:58,116
Almost everyone who sees
them leave assumes the Amish

21
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:02,936
way of life is finally dying out under
the pressure of modern secular society,

22
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:05,519
and that assumption is completely wrong.

23
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:08,496
They are not leaving because
their culture is shrinking.

24
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:11,396
They are leaving because
their numbers are exploding faster

25
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:14,200
than the American
landscape can contain them.

26
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:16,536
The demographic reality of the Amish

27
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:20,596
is one of the most astonishing
population stories in modern history.

28
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:21,936
A century ago,

29
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:24,716
the total Amish
population in North America

30
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:27,840
was estimated at barely
five thousand people.

31
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:29,496
By the year 2000,

32
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:33,136
that figure reached approximately
one hundred and sixty-five thousand.

33
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:34,096
Today,

34
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:37,996
according to census research from the
Young Center for Anabaptist and Pietist

35
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:40,196
Studies at Elizabethtown College,

36
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:43,836
the Amish population has surpassed
four hundred thousand individuals

37
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,636
across thirty-two states.

38
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:48,736
Their numbers double roughly
every twenty-two years.

39
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:53,296
While birth rates across the Western world
have plummeted below replacement levels,

40
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:57,756
the Amish maintain an average family
size of seven to nine children,

41
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:02,036
coupled with a retention rate where more
than eighty-five percent of young adults

42
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:04,840
choose lifelong baptism into the church.

43
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:09,076
Consider how an ordinary American
family handles relocation.

44
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:12,316
You pack your belongings because
of a corporate job transfer,

45
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:14,256
a promotion in a distant city,

46
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:17,736
or a desire for warmer
weather and lower income taxes.

47
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:20,216
You move as an isolated nuclear unit,

48
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:21,536
rent a moving truck,

49
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:24,096
buy a house in a planned
suburban development,

50
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:27,276
and immediately integrate
into the local utility grid,

51
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:30,180
internet networks,
and municipal school districts.

52
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:33,696
Your relocation is
an individual economic transaction

53
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:37,440
designed to optimize personal
comfort and career mobility.

54
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,883
Why would thousands of deeply
traditional families walk away

55
00:02:40,967 --> 00:02:44,743
from the most prosperous, productive
farmland on the eastern seaboard,

56
00:02:44,827 --> 00:02:48,387
soil their ancestors cleared
by hand three hundred years ago?

57
00:02:48,487 --> 00:02:51,323
What is actually driving
this mass migration,

58
00:02:51,407 --> 00:02:55,227
and where is America's fastest-
growing traditional community going?

59
00:02:55,507 --> 00:02:58,703
The conventional assumption
made by outside observers

60
00:02:58,787 --> 00:03:02,423
is that the Amish are being forced
out by religious persecution,

61
00:03:02,507 --> 00:03:03,383
poverty,

62
00:03:03,467 --> 00:03:07,227
or the inevitable drift
of their youth into modern secular life.

63
00:03:07,327 --> 00:03:10,087
That explanation is completely backwards.

64
00:03:10,287 --> 00:03:13,983
The Amish exodus is governed
not by secular assimilation,

65
00:03:14,067 --> 00:03:18,483
but by the relentless collision between
explosive demographic compounding

66
00:03:18,567 --> 00:03:22,963
and the non-negotiable spiritual
requirement of agrarian isolation.

67
00:03:23,047 --> 00:03:25,983
Under the unwritten communal
code known as the Ordnung,

68
00:03:26,067 --> 00:03:29,443
physical labor on the soil
is not merely an occupation,

69
00:03:29,527 --> 00:03:33,103
it is the protective spiritual
vessel that preserves humility,

70
00:03:33,187 --> 00:03:34,383
family cohesion,

71
00:03:34,467 --> 00:03:36,927
and separation from the secular world.

72
00:03:37,087 --> 00:03:40,703
When soaring land prices and suburban
sprawl make farming economically

73
00:03:40,787 --> 00:03:43,123
impossible in their historic heartland,

74
00:03:43,207 --> 00:03:47,387
the community cannot simply adapt
by becoming suburban commuters.

75
00:03:47,507 --> 00:03:49,423
To preserve the soul of their faith,

76
00:03:49,507 --> 00:03:53,947
they must dismantle their lives and
recreate the frontier in distant states.

77
00:03:54,207 --> 00:03:56,723
To understand the magnitude
of this departure,

78
00:03:56,807 --> 00:03:59,623
you have to appreciate what
Lancaster County represents

79
00:03:59,707 --> 00:04:01,483
in the Anabaptist memory.

80
00:04:01,567 --> 00:04:03,443
In the early eighteenth century,

81
00:04:03,527 --> 00:04:08,243
Swiss German Anabaptist refugees
fled severe religious persecution,

82
00:04:08,327 --> 00:04:09,283
imprisonment,

83
00:04:09,367 --> 00:04:11,163
and execution in Europe.

84
00:04:11,247 --> 00:04:15,463
Invited by William Penn under
his promise of absolute religious freedom,

85
00:04:15,547 --> 00:04:16,963
they settled in the lush,

86
00:04:17,047 --> 00:04:20,303
limestone-rich valleys
of southeastern Pennsylvania.

87
00:04:20,387 --> 00:04:22,603
There, they found some
of the most fertile,

88
00:04:22,687 --> 00:04:25,787
non-irrigated agricultural
land on the planet.

89
00:04:25,967 --> 00:04:27,223
For generations,

90
00:04:27,307 --> 00:04:30,427
Lancaster County served
as an agrarian fortress.

91
00:04:30,747 --> 00:04:34,683
The Amish community built an entirely
self-contained rural society

92
00:04:34,767 --> 00:04:36,303
based on family farming,

93
00:04:36,387 --> 00:04:37,463
draft horses,

94
00:04:37,547 --> 00:04:38,483
mutual aid,

95
00:04:38,567 --> 00:04:40,683
and strict separation from the world.

96
00:04:40,767 --> 00:04:42,743
They rejected grid electricity,

97
00:04:42,827 --> 00:04:44,743
automobiles, television,

98
00:04:44,827 --> 00:04:46,323
and public high schools,

99
00:04:46,407 --> 00:04:50,943
believing that modern consumer technology
naturally eroded family dependence

100
00:04:51,027 --> 00:04:52,607
and communal humility.

101
00:04:52,787 --> 00:04:54,043
In this fertile valley,

102
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:58,143
a father could farm eighty
acres with Belgian draft horses,

103
00:04:58,227 --> 00:04:59,563
raise ten children,

104
00:04:59,647 --> 00:05:03,887
and pass the land down to his sons
with complete economic independence.

105
00:05:04,287 --> 00:05:08,623
That system worked flawlessly as long
as there was open ground to clear.

106
00:05:08,707 --> 00:05:12,403
But the very success of the Amish
lifestyle created an insurmountable

107
00:05:12,487 --> 00:05:13,983
mathematical trap.

108
00:05:14,067 --> 00:05:17,356
In a society where every
family averages eight children,

109
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:21,896
a community of ten thousand people becomes
twenty thousand in a single generation,

110
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:23,516
forty thousand in the next,

111
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,640
and eighty thousand soon after.

112
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:29,536
When an Amish farmer with eighty
acres has four or five sons,

113
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,856
all of whom expect to become farmers,

114
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:34,076
simple arithmetic breaks down.

115
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:38,940
You cannot divide an eighty-acre dairy
farm into five viable family farms.

116
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:44,560
Compounding this internal population
pressure was an external demographic wave.

117
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:46,700
Over the last four decades,

118
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:49,876
Lancaster County was absorbed
into the expanding suburban

119
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:51,936
commuter belts of Philadelphia,

120
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:53,816
Harrisburg, and Baltimore.

121
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:57,536
Prime farmland was rapidly
purchased by commercial developers

122
00:05:57,620 --> 00:05:59,516
to build housing subdivisions,

123
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,176
commercial shopping centers,

124
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:02,940
and highway corridors.

125
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:07,496
Simultaneously, the county became
a major global tourist destination,

126
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:11,916
drawing millions of visitors eager to see
horse-drawn buggies and picturesque stone

127
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:12,940
barns.

128
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:16,856
The collision of suburban
development and agricultural scarcity

129
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:20,680
caused farmland prices
in Lancaster County to skyrocket.

130
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:24,736
Agricultural land that once sold
for a few thousand dollars an acre

131
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:27,816
climbed to fifteen thousand,
twenty-five thousand,

132
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:32,096
and in some prime locations, more than
thirty-five thousand dollars an acre.

133
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:35,376
For a young twenty-one-year-old
Amish man seeking to establish

134
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:37,416
an eighty-acre dairy farm,

135
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:40,520
the capital requirement
became astronomical.

136
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:42,016
Purchasing land,

137
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:44,476
constructing a traditional bank barn,

138
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,776
acquiring a herd of dairy cows,

139
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:49,176
and purchasing horse-drawn machinery

140
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:53,120
routinely required two to three
million dollars in cash.

141
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:57,316
Because few young couples possessed
millions of dollars in capital,

142
00:06:57,400 --> 00:07:01,560
an unprecedented cultural crisis
erupted in Lancaster County.

143
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:03,096
Unable to buy farms,

144
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:06,236
thousands of young Amish men
were forced off the soil.

145
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:10,696
They transitioned into non-farm
entrepreneurship and cottage industries.

146
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:12,476
They opened woodworking shops,

147
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,736
built storage sheds and gazebos,

148
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:16,756
worked in commercial roofing crews,

149
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:18,716
manufactured outdoor furniture,

150
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:22,240
and operated retail quilt
stands catering to tourists.

151
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:24,796
Today, researchers at Elizabethtown

152
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:29,756
College document that fewer than one-third
of adult Amish men in Lancaster County

153
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,840
still make their primary
living by farming the soil.

154
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:35,656
More than two-thirds
work in commercial trades,

155
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:38,056
construction, and manufacturing.

156
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:42,016
While these small businesses
generated substantial financial wealth,

157
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:46,736
they created profound anxiety among
church elders and traditional bishops.

158
00:07:46,820 --> 00:07:48,356
To the outside observer,

159
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:51,844
an Amish carpenter operating
a thriving furniture business

160
00:07:51,928 --> 00:07:54,948
looks like a model
of traditional American success.

161
00:07:55,108 --> 00:07:56,984
To a conservative Amish bishop,

162
00:07:57,068 --> 00:08:00,328
it looked like a slow
spiritual catastrophe.

163
00:08:00,788 --> 00:08:02,224
The reason was simple:

164
00:08:02,308 --> 00:08:06,204
the farm was the protective wall
that kept the secular world outside.

165
00:08:06,288 --> 00:08:09,224
When an Amish man worked
his own fields with his sons,

166
00:08:09,308 --> 00:08:11,864
the family spent twelve
hours a day together,

167
00:08:11,948 --> 00:08:14,224
isolated from secular conversation,

168
00:08:14,308 --> 00:08:15,304
pop culture,

169
00:08:15,388 --> 00:08:17,184
and worldly temptations.

170
00:08:17,268 --> 00:08:20,824
But when an Amish man operates
a commercial construction crew,

171
00:08:20,908 --> 00:08:24,664
he must travel in motor vehicles
driven by non-Amish drivers,

172
00:08:24,748 --> 00:08:27,304
interact daily with secular contractors,

173
00:08:27,388 --> 00:08:29,704
negotiate municipal building codes,

174
00:08:29,788 --> 00:08:33,928
and carry battery-operated cellular
phones for business logistics.

175
00:08:34,088 --> 00:08:35,944
Inside commercial workshops,

176
00:08:36,028 --> 00:08:39,648
the boundary line between the church
and the world began to blur.

177
00:08:39,808 --> 00:08:41,783
To compete in modern markets,

178
00:08:41,867 --> 00:08:44,204
shops adopted hydraulic equipment,

179
00:08:44,288 --> 00:08:45,944
pneumatic power tools,

180
00:08:46,028 --> 00:08:47,484
diesel generators,

181
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:52,088
and computerized business services
managed by outside third parties.

182
00:08:52,328 --> 00:08:56,124
Young Amish workers were suddenly
earning large cash incomes,

183
00:08:56,208 --> 00:09:00,584
spending their days listening to secular
radio on construction job sites,

184
00:09:00,668 --> 00:09:02,844
and navigating suburban traffic.

185
00:09:02,928 --> 00:09:05,204
Traditional church leaders recognized

186
00:09:05,288 --> 00:09:08,524
that while the outward appearance
of the faith remained intact,

187
00:09:08,608 --> 00:09:11,244
the internal spiritual
discipline of the Ordnung

188
00:09:11,328 --> 00:09:15,148
was being slowly compromised
by daily commercial exposure.

189
00:09:15,368 --> 00:09:18,044
For conservative bishops
and concerned fathers,

190
00:09:18,128 --> 00:09:20,228
the conclusion was inescapable.

191
00:09:20,428 --> 00:09:24,824
You cannot maintain the soul of an old
order agrarian church without the soil.

192
00:09:24,908 --> 00:09:28,704
If a young generation could no longer
afford to farm in Lancaster County,

193
00:09:28,788 --> 00:09:31,388
then the community had
to leave Lancaster County.

194
00:09:31,488 --> 00:09:33,764
The only way to save
the culture was to recreate

195
00:09:33,848 --> 00:09:36,564
the conditions
of the eighteenth-century frontier

196
00:09:36,648 --> 00:09:40,388
in regions where farmland was
still cheap, quiet, and remote.

197
00:09:41,008 --> 00:09:44,804
The migration was not a chaotic,
disorganized retreat.

198
00:09:44,888 --> 00:09:48,884
It was executed with the meticulous
planning characteristic of Anabaptist

199
00:09:48,968 --> 00:09:50,668
communal organization.

200
00:09:50,988 --> 00:09:55,044
Church districts formed scouting
committees composed of trusted deacons,

201
00:09:55,128 --> 00:09:56,024
ministers,

202
00:09:56,108 --> 00:09:57,928
and experienced farmers.

203
00:09:58,128 --> 00:10:00,724
These scouts hired non-Amish drivers

204
00:10:00,808 --> 00:10:04,264
and traveled thousands
of miles across rural America,

205
00:10:04,348 --> 00:10:07,908
searching for regions that
met strict communal criteria:

206
00:10:08,068 --> 00:10:09,204
fertile soil,

207
00:10:09,288 --> 00:10:10,948
reliable rainfall,

208
00:10:11,048 --> 00:10:13,144
low local property taxes,

209
00:10:13,228 --> 00:10:14,984
affordable land prices,

210
00:10:15,068 --> 00:10:16,884
and local rural populations that

211
00:10:16,968 --> 00:10:19,868
would welcome traditional
agricultural neighbors.

212
00:10:20,268 --> 00:10:23,724
One of the primary destinations
chosen by migrating families

213
00:10:23,808 --> 00:10:26,408
was rural upstate and western New York.

214
00:10:26,588 --> 00:10:28,645
Regions like the Conewango Valley,

215
00:10:28,729 --> 00:10:29,965
St. Lawrence County,

216
00:10:30,049 --> 00:10:31,225
Chautauqua County,

217
00:10:31,309 --> 00:10:36,125
and the Mohawk Valley offered vast
stretches of underutilized dairy farmland.

218
00:10:36,209 --> 00:10:37,445
In these counties,

219
00:10:37,529 --> 00:10:41,405
where centuries of rural industrial
decline had driven younger secular

220
00:10:41,489 --> 00:10:42,945
generations away,

221
00:10:43,029 --> 00:10:45,765
productive agricultural
land could be purchased

222
00:10:45,849 --> 00:10:49,029
for two thousand to four
thousand dollars per acre,

223
00:10:49,189 --> 00:10:52,589
roughly one-tenth the cost
of land in Lancaster County.

224
00:10:53,029 --> 00:10:56,649
The scale of the migration
into New York State was historic.

225
00:10:56,789 --> 00:10:58,625
In the early nineteen seventies,

226
00:10:58,709 --> 00:11:02,065
New York was home to barely
a handful of Amish families.

227
00:11:02,149 --> 00:11:06,485
Today, New York hosts more than
twenty-three thousand Amish residents

228
00:11:06,569 --> 00:11:09,869
distributed across more than
sixty distinct settlements.

229
00:11:10,089 --> 00:11:14,405
Entire agricultural valleys that had been
abandoned by secular commercial farming

230
00:11:14,489 --> 00:11:17,469
were brought back to life
by horse-drawn plows.

231
00:11:17,689 --> 00:11:19,965
Abandoned dairy barns were repaired,

232
00:11:20,049 --> 00:11:21,905
stone silos were restored,

233
00:11:21,989 --> 00:11:26,249
and quiet country roads were repaved
to accommodate wooden buggy wheels.

234
00:11:26,849 --> 00:11:28,245
Simultaneously,

235
00:11:28,329 --> 00:11:31,429
a massive southern migration
pushed into Kentucky.

236
00:11:31,589 --> 00:11:33,125
Areas like Hart County,

237
00:11:33,209 --> 00:11:36,265
including the communities
of Munfordville and Horse Cave,

238
00:11:36,349 --> 00:11:39,245
alongside settlements
in Christian and Todd counties,

239
00:11:39,329 --> 00:11:42,285
became magnets for families
seeking fertile ground

240
00:11:42,369 --> 00:11:44,245
and extended growing seasons.

241
00:11:44,329 --> 00:11:45,925
According to census data,

242
00:11:46,009 --> 00:11:49,585
Kentucky now ranks among the top
states for Amish settlement,

243
00:11:49,669 --> 00:11:53,465
home to more than seventeen thousand
Amish residents across nearly sixty

244
00:11:53,549 --> 00:11:55,249
separate church districts.

245
00:11:55,369 --> 00:11:58,345
Similar daughter settlements
were established in Wisconsin,

246
00:11:58,429 --> 00:11:59,345
Missouri,

247
00:11:59,429 --> 00:12:01,865
Iowa, Minnesota, and Tennessee.

248
00:12:01,949 --> 00:12:05,645
If you value this kind of measured,
factual, investigative reporting

249
00:12:05,729 --> 00:12:09,965
on traditional cultures and the hidden
economic forces reshaping America,

250
00:12:10,049 --> 00:12:11,869
take a second to subscribe.

251
00:12:12,029 --> 00:12:16,265
It helps support independent research that
relies strictly on verified demographic

252
00:12:16,349 --> 00:12:18,009
and historical records.

253
00:12:18,349 --> 00:12:20,825
The physical process of relocation

254
00:12:20,909 --> 00:12:24,165
reveals the communal
discipline of the Amish world.

255
00:12:24,249 --> 00:12:28,149
An Amish family does not simply
pack a suitcase and move alone.

256
00:12:28,249 --> 00:12:31,685
The basic unit of Amish
life is the church district,

257
00:12:31,769 --> 00:12:35,325
an autonomous fellowship of twenty-
five to thirty-five families

258
00:12:35,409 --> 00:12:37,545
under the spiritual care of a bishop,

259
00:12:37,629 --> 00:12:38,625
two ministers,

260
00:12:38,709 --> 00:12:39,865
and a deacon.

261
00:12:39,949 --> 00:12:41,909
When a new settlement is founded,

262
00:12:42,009 --> 00:12:45,949
multiple related families move
together in coordinated waves.

263
00:12:46,069 --> 00:12:50,265
They hire chartered commercial flatbed
trucks to transport draft horses,

264
00:12:50,349 --> 00:12:51,429
dairy cattle,

265
00:12:51,513 --> 00:12:52,729
farming implements,

266
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,149
wood-burning stoves,

267
00:12:54,233 --> 00:12:55,853
and handmade furniture.

268
00:12:56,133 --> 00:12:58,429
Upon arriving in a new rural county,

269
00:12:58,513 --> 00:13:00,229
the families work collectively

270
00:13:00,313 --> 00:13:03,393
to establish their parallel
social infrastructure.

271
00:13:03,833 --> 00:13:06,069
They pool labor to raise barns,

272
00:13:06,153 --> 00:13:07,849
construct outhouses,

273
00:13:07,933 --> 00:13:09,249
drill water wells,

274
00:13:09,333 --> 00:13:12,312
and erect a one-room
parochial schoolhouse.

275
00:13:12,433 --> 00:13:15,869
The children leave the public
educational system entirely,

276
00:13:15,953 --> 00:13:20,469
attending community schools taught
by young Amish women who teach reading,

277
00:13:20,553 --> 00:13:22,209
writing, arithmetic,

278
00:13:22,293 --> 00:13:25,049
and German hymns through the eighth grade.

279
00:13:25,133 --> 00:13:27,669
Within months of arrival, an autonomous,

280
00:13:27,753 --> 00:13:31,449
self-sufficient church
district is fully operational,

281
00:13:31,533 --> 00:13:35,753
holding worship services in members'
homes on alternating Sundays.

282
00:13:36,053 --> 00:13:38,769
For many depressed rural American towns,

283
00:13:38,853 --> 00:13:43,928
the arrival of hundreds of Amish families
provided a major economic lifeline.

284
00:13:44,012 --> 00:13:46,729
In rural counties where
schools were closing

285
00:13:46,813 --> 00:13:49,029
and local main streets were shuttering,

286
00:13:49,113 --> 00:13:52,429
the Amish brought active
economic revitalization.

287
00:13:52,513 --> 00:13:54,889
They purchased decaying farmsteads,

288
00:13:54,973 --> 00:13:57,509
paid delinquent county property taxes,

289
00:13:57,593 --> 00:13:59,989
and established bustling sawmills,

290
00:14:00,073 --> 00:14:01,529
produce auctions,

291
00:14:01,613 --> 00:14:02,889
bulk food stores,

292
00:14:02,973 --> 00:14:04,393
and harness shops.

293
00:14:04,573 --> 00:14:06,649
Non-Amish hardware stores,

294
00:14:06,733 --> 00:14:08,929
feed mills, and veterinarians

295
00:14:09,013 --> 00:14:11,349
experienced significant business growth,

296
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:15,009
creating cooperative relationships
between traditional settlers

297
00:14:15,093 --> 00:14:17,153
and local secular residents.

298
00:14:17,413 --> 00:14:21,873
Yet this rapid migration has
also generated localized friction.

299
00:14:21,993 --> 00:14:24,189
In rural New York and Kentucky,

300
00:14:24,273 --> 00:14:27,509
local town councils and non-
Amish drivers often struggle

301
00:14:27,593 --> 00:14:32,469
with the sudden appearance of slow-moving
buggies on narrow, unlit rural highways,

302
00:14:32,553 --> 00:14:37,673
leading to traffic accidents and debates
over orange reflective safety triangles.

303
00:14:37,773 --> 00:14:39,329
In several jurisdictions,

304
00:14:39,413 --> 00:14:42,169
tensions erupted over
municipal building codes,

305
00:14:42,253 --> 00:14:43,509
septic regulations,

306
00:14:43,593 --> 00:14:47,289
and state mandates requiring
indoor plumbing and smoke detectors,

307
00:14:47,373 --> 00:14:51,089
which traditional Amish bishops view
as unwarranted government intrusion

308
00:14:51,173 --> 00:14:53,173
into religious domestic life.

309
00:14:53,633 --> 00:14:57,953
The emotional toll of this migration
is deeply felt inside the community.

310
00:14:58,073 --> 00:15:01,569
Leaving Lancaster County is
not merely a change of address,

311
00:15:01,653 --> 00:15:06,133
it is a painful severance from three
centuries of sacred family heritage.

312
00:15:06,313 --> 00:15:10,389
When a young family packs their belongings
for upstate New York or Kentucky,

313
00:15:10,473 --> 00:15:13,689
they are leaving behind the cemetery
plots where eight generations

314
00:15:13,773 --> 00:15:18,153
of their direct ancestors lie buried
under simple fieldstone markers.

315
00:15:18,273 --> 00:15:20,169
They are separating elderly grandparents

316
00:15:20,253 --> 00:15:22,989
from their grandchildren
by hundreds of miles

317
00:15:23,073 --> 00:15:25,943
in a society where
telephone calls are restricted

318
00:15:26,027 --> 00:15:30,347
and long-distance travel requires
hiring costly non-Amish drivers.

319
00:15:30,527 --> 00:15:33,323
The move often divides extended families.

320
00:15:33,407 --> 00:15:37,183
More progressive Amish families who
choose to remain in Lancaster County

321
00:15:37,267 --> 00:15:40,203
continue to adapt
to commercial entrepreneurship,

322
00:15:40,287 --> 00:15:44,887
operating successful multi-million
dollar construction and retail businesses.

323
00:15:45,067 --> 00:15:48,003
Meanwhile,
the conservative families who depart

324
00:15:48,087 --> 00:15:51,707
view their relocation as
an act of spiritual survival.

325
00:15:51,807 --> 00:15:55,523
They deliberately trade modern business
wealth and commercial convenience

326
00:15:55,607 --> 00:15:57,423
for rugged frontier farming,

327
00:15:57,507 --> 00:16:01,807
choosing poverty and physical
isolation over cultural assimilation.

328
00:16:02,207 --> 00:16:05,007
Here lies the great
irony of the Amish story.

329
00:16:05,187 --> 00:16:08,223
Outside observers frequently
look at the horse and buggy,

330
00:16:08,307 --> 00:16:09,923
the plain denim clothes,

331
00:16:10,007 --> 00:16:11,923
and the absence of electricity,

332
00:16:12,007 --> 00:16:15,703
and assume they are looking at a dying,
fragile relic of the past

333
00:16:15,787 --> 00:16:18,803
that is slowly being crushed
by modern civilization.

334
00:16:18,887 --> 00:16:19,963
In reality,

335
00:16:20,047 --> 00:16:22,427
the exact opposite is taking place.

336
00:16:22,607 --> 00:16:24,423
Modern secular society,

337
00:16:24,507 --> 00:16:27,623
with its falling birth rates
and disintegrating families,

338
00:16:27,707 --> 00:16:30,803
is watching a traditional
community grow so fast

339
00:16:30,887 --> 00:16:34,487
that it is outgrowing the physical
boundaries of its own homeland.

340
00:16:34,787 --> 00:16:39,303
The Amish are leaving Lancaster County
not because their experiment failed,

341
00:16:39,387 --> 00:16:41,587
but because it succeeded too well.

342
00:16:41,767 --> 00:16:46,547
They proved that a community built
on shared faith, unconditional mutual aid,

343
00:16:46,667 --> 00:16:50,563
disciplined family structure,
and contentment with simple labor can

344
00:16:50,647 --> 00:16:55,723
outpopulate and outcompete the material
comforts of modern secular America. When

345
00:16:55,807 --> 00:16:59,743
forced to choose between the financial
wealth of suburban commercial business

346
00:16:59,827 --> 00:17:02,203
and the spiritual protection of the soil,

347
00:17:02,287 --> 00:17:04,707
thousands of families chose the soil.

348
00:17:05,167 --> 00:17:08,003
If current demographic
trajectories continue,

349
00:17:08,087 --> 00:17:12,403
researchers at the Young Center project
that the North American Amish population

350
00:17:12,487 --> 00:17:16,843
will approach one million individuals
by the middle of the twenty-first century.

351
00:17:16,927 --> 00:17:21,503
As older settlements in Pennsylvania
and Ohio reach complete saturation,

352
00:17:21,587 --> 00:17:25,207
the map of rural America
will continue to be redrawn.

353
00:17:25,307 --> 00:17:29,263
New daughter settlements will continue
to spread across the hills of New York,

354
00:17:29,347 --> 00:17:30,883
the valleys of Kentucky,

355
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:32,863
and the plains of the Midwest,

356
00:17:32,947 --> 00:17:38,387
carving out new sanctuaries of traditional
peace in an increasingly noisy world.

357
00:17:38,807 --> 00:17:42,823
When you look at your own life and the
rapid pace of the modern world around you,

358
00:17:42,907 --> 00:17:46,283
how many compromises have you
made for the sake of convenience,

359
00:17:46,367 --> 00:17:48,943
technology, and economic advancement?

360
00:17:49,027 --> 00:17:51,663
What would it take for you
to walk away from your home,

361
00:17:51,747 --> 00:17:52,783
your career,

362
00:17:52,867 --> 00:17:54,043
and your comfort

363
00:17:54,127 --> 00:17:57,347
simply to protect the spiritual
foundation of your family?

364
00:17:57,567 --> 00:18:01,283
What is your perspective
on the Amish migration across America?

365
00:18:01,367 --> 00:18:05,983
Can traditional agrarian communities
survive indefinitely in modern America,

366
00:18:06,067 --> 00:18:09,087
or will the secular world
eventually catch up to them?

367
00:18:09,207 --> 00:18:11,604
Share your perspective
in the comments below.

